@lang en
IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `ca-interpretation-nouns`
IMPORT `ca-interpretation-rules`
IMPORT `ca-interpretation-reading`

-- ca-interpretation-definitions.l4
--
-- The Interpretation Act (Canada), R.S.C., 1985, c. I-21: the defined terms of section 2(1) ("In this Act,") and section 35(1) ("In every
-- enactment,").  Pass 2.
--
-- HOW A DEFINITION IS ENCODED HERE.  Each entry of the Act is a constant of type `A definition`: the terms it defines, its section, the
-- word the Act uses (means, includes, ...), the members it names, what it excludes, and what it points at.  The members and pointers are the
-- Act's own words, copied from the text.  `the term defined by` d `covers` x then answers the question a reader asks of any entry,
-- "is x within this term?", with the one rule the words themselves give:
--   * x is named, and the Act says "means" or "includes": yes;
--   * x is named as excluded (corporation does not include a partnership ...): no;
--   * x is not named and the Act says "means": no, because "means" gives the whole meaning;
--   * x is not named and the Act says "includes" (or "does not include", or points at another term): the Act does not say, so the
--     answer is a refusal, never FALSE.
-- Where a definition turns on facts a person could state (a transmission's frequency, how many justices, whether a bank is listed), the
-- entry also has a function over those facts.  Borrowed terms (the Bank Act, the Oceans Act, the Criminal Code) are asked as facts.
-- Plain gloss of every term is in its heading comment.

§ `The table of definitions: its types and its one rule`

DECLARE `How a definition speaks` IS ONE OF
    `means`
    `includes`
    `means, and also includes`
    `for greater certainty, includes`
    `does not include`
    `has the same meaning as`
    `shall be construed as relating to`
    `shall be understood to relate to`

DECLARE `A definition` HAS
    `the terms`         IS A LIST OF STRING
    `its section`       IS A STRING
    `how it speaks`     IS A `How a definition speaks`
    `what it names`     IS A LIST OF STRING
    `what it excludes`  IS A LIST OF STRING
    `what it points at` IS A MAYBE STRING

-- src:15 | 2 (1) In this Act,
-- src:275 | 35 (1) In every enactment,
@ref Interpretation Act s 2(1) (src:15) and s 35(1) (src:275): a definition that includes says what it includes
GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN a
`a definition that includes does not say that nothing else is covered` MEANS
    REFUSE "a definition that includes does not say that nothing else is covered"

-- src:15 | 2 (1) In this Act,
-- src:275 | 35 (1) In every enactment,
@ref Interpretation Act s 2(1) (src:15) and s 35(1) (src:275): a definition that does not include says what it excludes
GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN a
`a definition that does not include does not say what else it covers` MEANS
    REFUSE "a definition that does not include does not say what else it covers"

-- src:15 | 2 (1) In this Act,
-- src:275 | 35 (1) In every enactment,
@ref Interpretation Act s 2(1) (src:15) and s 35(1) (src:275): a definition that points at another term does not list members
GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN a
`a definition that points at another term does not list what the term covers` MEANS
    REFUSE "a definition that points at another term does not list what the term covers"

-- What the definition says of a thing it does not name.
-- src:15 | 2 (1) In this Act,
-- src:275 | 35 (1) In every enactment,
@ref Interpretation Act s 2(1) (src:15) and s 35(1) (src:275)
GIVEN d IS A `A definition`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`what the definition says of a thing it does not name` d MEANS
    CONSIDER d's `how it speaks`
    WHEN `means`                              THEN FALSE
    WHEN `means, and also includes`           THEN FALSE
    WHEN `includes`                           THEN `a definition that includes does not say that nothing else is covered`
    WHEN `for greater certainty, includes`    THEN `a definition that includes does not say that nothing else is covered`
    WHEN `does not include`                   THEN `a definition that does not include does not say what else it covers`
    WHEN `has the same meaning as`            THEN `a definition that points at another term does not list what the term covers`
    WHEN `shall be construed as relating to`  THEN `a definition that points at another term does not list what the term covers`
    WHEN `shall be understood to relate to`   THEN `a definition that points at another term does not list what the term covers`

-- src:15 | 2 (1) In this Act,
-- src:275 | 35 (1) In every enactment,
@ref Interpretation Act s 2(1) (src:15) and s 35(1) (src:275)
GIVEN d IS A `A definition`
      x IS A STRING
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the term defined by` d `covers` x MEANS
    BRANCH IF elem x (d's `what it names`)    THEN TRUE
           IF elem x (d's `what it excludes`) THEN FALSE
           OTHERWISE `what the definition says of a thing it does not name` d

§ `Section 2(1) and section 35(1): where the definitions apply`

-- "In this Act," (s 2(1)) and "In every enactment," (s 35(1)): the places in which the definitions speak.
DECLARE `Where a definition is being applied` IS ONE OF
    `in the Interpretation Act itself`
    `in another enactment`
    `somewhere that is not an enactment`

-- src:15 | 2 (1) In this Act,
@ref Interpretation Act s 2(1) (src:15)
GIVEN w IS A `Where a definition is being applied`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`a definition of section 2(1) applies` w MEANS
    CONSIDER w
    WHEN `in the Interpretation Act itself`  THEN TRUE
    WHEN `in another enactment`              THEN `section 2(1) defines words for this Act and does not say whether the definitions reach another enactment`
    WHEN `somewhere that is not an enactment` THEN `section 2(1) defines words for this Act and does not say whether the definitions reach another enactment`

-- src:15 | 2 (1) In this Act,
@ref Interpretation Act s 2(1) (src:15): the words are "In this Act"
GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN a
`section 2(1) defines words for this Act and does not say whether the definitions reach another enactment` MEANS
    REFUSE "section 2(1) defines words for this Act and does not say whether the definitions reach another enactment"

-- src:275 | 35 (1) In every enactment,
-- src:29 | 3 (1) Every provision of this Act applies, unless a contrary intention appears, to every enactment, whether enacted before or after the commencement of this Act.
-- src:31 | (2) The provisions of this Act apply to the interpretation of this Act.
@ref Interpretation Act s 35(1) (src:275) with s 3(1) (src:29) and s 3(2) (src:31)
GIVEN w IS A `Where a definition is being applied`
      `a contrary intention appears` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`a definition of section 35(1) applies` w `unless` `a contrary intention appears` MEANS
    CONSIDER w
    WHEN `in the Interpretation Act itself`   THEN `a provision of the Act applies to the interpretation of the Act`
    WHEN `in another enactment`               THEN `a provision of the Act applies to an enactment unless` `a contrary intention appears`
    WHEN `somewhere that is not an enactment` THEN `section 35(1) defines words for every enactment and does not say whether the definitions reach anything else`

-- src:275 | 35 (1) In every enactment,
@ref Interpretation Act s 35(1) (src:275): the words are "In every enactment"
GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN a
`section 35(1) defines words for every enactment and does not say whether the definitions reach anything else` MEANS
    REFUSE "section 35(1) defines words for every enactment and does not say whether the definitions reach anything else"

§ `Section 3(1): the Act applies to every enactment, by kind of instrument`

-- Plain gloss: every provision of the Act applies to every enactment, unless a contrary intention appears, whether the enactment was
-- enacted before or after the Act.  "Enactment" is an Act or a regulation or any portion of either, and "Act" is an Act of Parliament
-- (s 2(1)), so the instruments section 3(1) names are the kinds that section 2(1) names.  An Act of a legislature (a provincial Act, say) is
-- not an "Act" in this Act's sense, so it is not an enactment, and section 3(1) says nothing of whether any provision applies to it.
-- That is a silence in the text (S-3-1-KIND in NOTES.md section 3), and the answer for it is the named refusal below.
-- The test of what an enactment is stays in the entry for "enactment" (`is an enactment within section 2(1)`); it is called, not copied.
-- The contrary intention is asked once, here and in the gate `a provision of the Act applies to an enactment unless` (convention C-3-1-GATE).
-- src:29 | 3 (1) Every provision of this Act applies, unless a contrary intention appears, to every enactment, whether enacted before or after the commencement of this Act.
-- src:16 | Act means an Act of Parliament; (loi)
-- src:18 | enactment means an Act or regulation or any portion of an Act or regulation; (texte)
@ref Interpretation Act s 3(1) (src:29), s 2(1) "Act" (src:16) and s 2(1) "enactment" (src:18)
GIVEN k IS A `A kind of instrument`
      `a contrary intention appears` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the provisions of the Act apply to an instrument of the kind` k `unless` `a contrary intention appears` MEANS
    IF   `is an enactment within section 2(1)` k
    THEN `a provision of the Act applies to an enactment unless` `a contrary intention appears`
    ELSE `section 3(1) applies the provisions of the Act to every enactment and says nothing of an instrument that is not an enactment`

-- src:29 | 3 (1) Every provision of this Act applies, unless a contrary intention appears, to every enactment, whether enacted before or after the commencement of this Act.
@ref Interpretation Act s 3(1) (src:29): an instrument that is not an enactment is not addressed
GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN a
`section 3(1) applies the provisions of the Act to every enactment and says nothing of an instrument that is not an enactment` MEANS
    REFUSE "section 3(1) applies the provisions of the Act to every enactment and says nothing of an instrument that is not an enactment"

§ `Section 2(1): the definitions`

§§ `s 2(1) "Act"`

-- Plain gloss: in this Act, "Act" is an Act of Parliament and nothing else.
-- src:16 | Act means an Act of Parliament; (loi)
@ref Interpretation Act s 2(1) "Act" (src:16)
GIVETH A `A definition`
`the definition of the term Act in section 2(1)` MEANS
    `A definition`
        WITH `the terms` IS LIST "Act"
             `its section` IS "2(1)"
             `how it speaks` IS `means`
             `what it names` IS LIST "an Act of Parliament"
             `what it excludes` IS EMPTY
             `what it points at` IS NOTHING

-- src:16 | Act means an Act of Parliament; (loi)
@ref Interpretation Act s 2(1) "Act" (src:16)
GIVEN k IS A `A kind of instrument`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`is an Act within section 2(1)` k MEANS
    CONSIDER k
    WHEN `an Act of Parliament`                      THEN TRUE
    WHEN `an Act of a legislature`                   THEN FALSE
    WHEN `a regulation`                              THEN FALSE
    WHEN `a portion of an Act of Parliament`         THEN FALSE
    WHEN `a portion of a regulation`                 THEN FALSE
    WHEN `an instrument of none of these kinds`      THEN FALSE

§§ `s 2(1) "enact"`

-- Plain gloss: to enact includes to issue, to make and to establish.  Other verbs are not said to be outside it.
-- src:17 | enact includes to issue, make or establish; (Version anglaise seulement)
@ref Interpretation Act s 2(1) "enact" (src:17)
GIVETH A `A definition`
`the definition of the term enact` MEANS
    `A definition`
        WITH `the terms` IS LIST "enact"
             `its section` IS "2(1)"
             `how it speaks` IS `includes`
             `what it names` IS LIST "issue", "make", "establish"
             `what it excludes` IS EMPTY
             `what it points at` IS NOTHING

§§ `s 2(1) "enactment"`

-- Plain gloss: an enactment is an Act or a regulation or any portion of either.
-- src:18 | enactment means an Act or regulation or any portion of an Act or regulation; (texte)
@ref Interpretation Act s 2(1) "enactment" (src:18)
GIVETH A `A definition`
`the definition of the term enactment` MEANS
    `A definition`
        WITH `the terms` IS LIST "enactment"
             `its section` IS "2(1)"
             `how it speaks` IS `means`
             `what it names` IS LIST "an Act", "a regulation", "any portion of an Act or regulation"
             `what it excludes` IS EMPTY
             `what it points at` IS NOTHING

-- src:18 | enactment means an Act or regulation or any portion of an Act or regulation; (texte)
@ref Interpretation Act s 2(1) "enactment" (src:18)
GIVEN k IS A `A kind of instrument`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`is an enactment within section 2(1)` k MEANS
    CONSIDER k
    WHEN `an Act of Parliament`                      THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a regulation`                              THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a portion of an Act of Parliament`         THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a portion of a regulation`                 THEN TRUE
    WHEN `an Act of a legislature`                   THEN FALSE
    WHEN `an instrument of none of these kinds`      THEN FALSE

§§ `s 2(1) "public officer"`

-- Plain gloss: a public officer includes a person in the federal public administration who is authorized by or under an enactment to
-- do or enforce a thing or exercise a power, or on whom a duty is imposed by or under an enactment.
-- FORK F-PUBLIC-OFFICER: does "in the federal public administration" qualify both limbs ("who is authorized ... or on whom a duty is imposed")?
-- The text does not choose.  Where the two readings agree (a person in the federal public administration who is authorized or charged with a
-- duty) the answer is TRUE.  Where they differ (a person outside it on whom a duty is imposed) the answer is the named refusal below.
-- src:19 | public officer includes any person in the federal public administration who is authorized by or under an enactment to do or enforce the doing of an act or thing or to exercise a power, or on whom a duty is imposed by or under an enactment; (fonctionnaire public)
@ref Interpretation Act s 2(1) "public officer" (src:19)
GIVETH A `A definition`
`the definition of the term public officer` MEANS
    `A definition`
        WITH `the terms` IS LIST "public officer"
             `its section` IS "2(1)"
             `how it speaks` IS `includes`
             `what it names` IS LIST "any person in the federal public administration who is authorized by or under an enactment to do or enforce the doing of an act or thing or to exercise a power, or on whom a duty is imposed by or under an enactment"
             `what it excludes` IS EMPTY
             `what it points at` IS NOTHING

-- src:19 | public officer includes any person in the federal public administration who is authorized by or under an enactment to do or enforce the doing of an act or thing or to exercise a power, or on whom a duty is imposed by or under an enactment; (fonctionnaire public)
@ref Interpretation Act s 2(1) "public officer" (src:19)
GIVEN `the person is in the federal public administration` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is authorized by or under an enactment to do or enforce the doing of an act or thing or to exercise a power` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a duty is imposed on the person by or under an enactment` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`is a public officer within section 2(1) where` `the person is in the federal public administration` `and is authorized` `the person is authorized by or under an enactment to do or enforce the doing of an act or thing or to exercise a power` `or has a duty imposed` `a duty is imposed on the person by or under an enactment` MEANS
    IF       `the person is in the federal public administration`
         AND (   `the person is authorized by or under an enactment to do or enforce the doing of an act or thing or to exercise a power`
              OR `a duty is imposed on the person by or under an enactment`)
    THEN TRUE
    ELSE `section 2(1) says a public officer includes such a person and does not say that no one else is one, nor whether a duty imposed on a person outside the federal public administration suffices`

-- src:19 | public officer includes any person in the federal public administration who is authorized by or under an enactment to do or enforce the doing of an act or thing or to exercise a power, or on whom a duty is imposed by or under an enactment; (fonctionnaire public)
@ref Interpretation Act s 2(1) "public officer" (src:19): the definition includes and is silent on the rest
GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN a
`section 2(1) says a public officer includes such a person and does not say that no one else is one, nor whether a duty imposed on a person outside the federal public administration suffices` MEANS
    REFUSE "section 2(1) says a public officer includes such a person and does not say that no one else is one, nor whether a duty imposed on a person outside the federal public administration suffices"

§§ `s 2(1) "repeal"`

-- Plain gloss: to repeal includes to revoke and to cancel.
-- src:23 | repeal includes revoke or cancel. (Version anglaise seulement)
@ref Interpretation Act s 2(1) "repeal" (src:23)
GIVETH A `A definition`
`the definition of the term repeal` MEANS
    `A definition`
        WITH `the terms` IS LIST "repeal"
             `its section` IS "2(1)"
             `how it speaks` IS `includes`
             `what it names` IS LIST "revoke", "cancel"
             `what it excludes` IS EMPTY
             `what it points at` IS NOTHING

§ `Section 35(1): the types its entries share`

-- The five zones of the sea (contiguous zone, continental shelf, exclusive economic zone, internal waters, territorial sea) are each defined
-- twice over, once "in relation to Canada" and once "in relation to any other state"; each entry below is a function of `A state`.
DECLARE `A state` IS ONE OF
    `Canada as a state`
    `a state other than Canada`

-- What a zone of the sea is, in relation to one state: the thing, how its extent is fixed, and what the Act says it also takes in.
DECLARE `What a zone is` HAS
    `what it is`            IS A STRING
    `how it is fixed`       IS A STRING
    `what it also includes` IS A LIST OF STRING

-- The kinds of day that the definition of "holiday" lists.
DECLARE `A kind of day` IS ONE OF
    `a Sunday`
    `New Year’s Day`
    `Good Friday`
    `Easter Monday`
    `Christmas Day`
    `the birthday of the reigning Sovereign`
    `the day fixed by proclamation for the celebration of the birthday of the reigning Sovereign`
    `Victoria Day`
    `Canada Day`
    `Labour Day, the first Monday in September`
    `the National Day for Truth and Reconciliation, September 30`
    `Remembrance Day`
    `a day appointed by proclamation to be observed as a day of general prayer or mourning or day of public rejoicing or thanksgiving`
    `a day appointed by proclamation of the lieutenant governor of a province to be observed as a public holiday or as a day of general prayer or mourning or day of public rejoicing or thanksgiving within the province`
    `a non-juridical day by virtue of an Act of the legislature of a province`
    `a day appointed to be observed as a civic holiday by resolution of the council or other authority charged with the administration of the civic or municipal affairs of a city, town, municipality or other organized district`
    `a Saturday`
    `any other day`

-- The systems that "telecommunications" lists.
DECLARE `A system of emission, transmission or reception` IS ONE OF
    `a wire system`
    `a cable system`
    `a radio system`
    `an optical system`
    `another electromagnetic system`
    `a similar technical system`
    `a system of none of these kinds`

-- The modes that "writing" lists.
DECLARE `A mode of representing words` IS ONE OF
    `words printed`
    `words typewritten`
    `words painted`
    `words engraved`
    `words lithographed`
    `words photographed`
    `words represented or reproduced by another mode of representing or reproducing words in visible form`
    `words that are not in visible form`

§ `Section 35(1): the definitions, in the order of the text`

§§ `s 35(1) "Act"`

-- Plain gloss: where an enactment speaks of an Act of a legislature, "Act" includes a law of the legislature of Yukon, of the Northwest
-- Territories or of Nunavut.  (The text writes "of Yukon, of the Northwest Territories or for Nunavut"; the list below spells each out.)
-- src:276 | Act, in respect of an Act of a legislature, includes a law of the Legislature of Yukon, of the Northwest Territories or for Nunavut; (loi provinciale)
@ref Interpretation Act s 35(1) "Act" (src:276)
GIVETH A `A definition`
`the definition of the term Act in an enactment, in respect of an Act of a legislature` MEANS
    `A definition`
        WITH `the terms` IS LIST "Act"
             `its section` IS "35(1)"
             `how it speaks` IS `includes`
             `what it names` IS LIST "a law of the Legislature of Yukon"
                                    , "a law of the Legislature of the Northwest Territories"
                                    , "a law of the Legislature for Nunavut"
             `what it excludes` IS EMPTY
             `what it points at` IS NOTHING

§§ `s 35(1) "bank"`

-- Plain gloss: a bank is one listed in Schedule I or II to the Bank Act.  The listing is a fact about the bank; the Bank Act is not in
-- the text.
-- src:277 | bank means a bank listed in Schedule I or II to the Bank Act; (banque)
@ref Interpretation Act s 35(1) "bank" (src:277)
GIVETH A `A definition`
`the definition of the term bank` MEANS
    `A definition`
        WITH `the terms` IS LIST "bank"
             `its section` IS "35(1)"
             `how it speaks` IS `means`
             `what it names` IS LIST "a bank listed in Schedule I or II to the Bank Act"
             `what it excludes` IS EMPTY
             `what it points at` IS JUST "the Bank Act"

-- src:277 | bank means a bank listed in Schedule I or II to the Bank Act; (banque)
@ref Interpretation Act s 35(1) "bank" (src:277)
GIVEN `the bank is listed in Schedule I or II to the Bank Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`is a bank within section 35(1) if` `the bank is listed in Schedule I or II to the Bank Act` MEANS
    `the bank is listed in Schedule I or II to the Bank Act`

§§ `s 35(1) "broadcasting"`

-- Plain gloss: broadcasting is any radiocommunication whose transmissions are meant to be received directly by the general public.
-- src:279 | broadcasting means any radiocommunication in which the transmissions are intended for direct reception by the general public; (radiodiffusion)
@ref Interpretation Act s 35(1) "broadcasting" (src:279)
GIVETH A `A definition`
`the definition of the term broadcasting` MEANS
    `A definition`
        WITH `the terms` IS LIST "broadcasting"
             `its section` IS "35(1)"
             `how it speaks` IS `means`
             `what it names` IS LIST "any radiocommunication in which the transmissions are intended for direct reception by the general public"
             `what it excludes` IS EMPTY
             `what it points at` IS NOTHING

-- src:279 | broadcasting means any radiocommunication in which the transmissions are intended for direct reception by the general public; (radiodiffusion)
@ref Interpretation Act s 35(1) "broadcasting" (src:279)
GIVEN `it is a radiocommunication` IS A BOOLEAN
      `its transmissions are intended for direct reception by the general public` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`is broadcasting within section 35(1) where` `it is a radiocommunication` `and` `its transmissions are intended for direct reception by the general public` MEANS
        `it is a radiocommunication`
    AND `its transmissions are intended for direct reception by the general public`

§§ `s 35(1) "Canada"`

