§§ `s 35(1) "Governor General in Council or Governor in Council"`

-- Plain gloss: the Governor General of Canada acting with the Queen's Privy Council for Canada, in any of three ways: on its advice, on its
-- advice and consent, or in conjunction with it.
-- FORK F-QUEENS: the text says "the Queen’s Privy Council for Canada" while the Sovereign is a King.  Taken: the body meant is the Privy
-- Council for Canada, under whatever style the reigning Sovereign gives it (the input below is that fact).  The other reading is that
-- only a body styled "Queen’s" counts.
DECLARE `How the Governor General acts with the Privy Council` IS ONE OF
    `by and with the advice of`
    `by and with the advice and consent of`
    `in conjunction with`
    `without`

-- src:304 | Governor General in Council or Governor in Council means the Governor General of Canada acting by and with the advice of, or by and with the advice and consent of, or in conjunction with the Queen’s Privy Council for Canada; (gouverneur en conseil ou gouverneur général en conseil)
@ref Interpretation Act s 35(1) "Governor General in Council or Governor in Council" (src:304)
GIVETH A `A definition`
`the definition of the term Governor in Council` MEANS
    `A definition`
        WITH `the terms` IS LIST "Governor General in Council"
                                , "Governor in Council"
             `its section` IS "35(1)"
             `how it speaks` IS `means`
             `what it names` IS LIST "the Governor General of Canada acting by and with the advice of, or by and with the advice and consent of, or in conjunction with the Queen’s Privy Council for Canada"
             `what it excludes` IS EMPTY
             `what it points at` IS NOTHING

-- src:304 | Governor General in Council or Governor in Council means the Governor General of Canada acting by and with the advice of, or by and with the advice and consent of, or in conjunction with the Queen’s Privy Council for Canada; (gouverneur en conseil ou gouverneur général en conseil)
@ref Interpretation Act s 35(1) "Governor General in Council or Governor in Council" (src:304)
GIVEN h IS A `How the Governor General acts with the Privy Council`
      `the body is the Privy Council for Canada, under whatever style the reigning Sovereign gives it` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the Governor General is the Governor in Council when acting` h `with a body for which` `the body is the Privy Council for Canada, under whatever style the reigning Sovereign gives it` MEANS
        `the body is the Privy Council for Canada, under whatever style the reigning Sovereign gives it`
    AND CONSIDER h
        WHEN `by and with the advice of`             THEN TRUE
        WHEN `by and with the advice and consent of` THEN TRUE
        WHEN `in conjunction with`                   THEN TRUE
        WHEN `without`                               THEN FALSE

