§§ `s 35(1) "holiday"`

-- Plain gloss: a holiday is any of the days the text lists, and no other day.  Sunday is listed and Saturday is not.
-- The days that carry a place are the two kinds of additional day, (a) and (b): a day a province's lieutenant governor appoints, or makes
-- non-juridical by an Act, is listed "in any province"; a civic holiday is listed "in any city, town, municipality or other organized
-- district".  The refusal below says what the text does not: whether such a day is a holiday for a thing done in another place.
-- The dates of the days the text dates are in the calendar module; this entry sorts the kinds.
-- FORK F-HOLIDAY-PLACE: the two kinds of additional day carry a place ("in any province", "in any city, town, municipality or other organized
-- district"), and neither section 26 nor this definition says where a thing "is done" for a time limit, or whether a day appointed for one
-- place is a holiday for a thing done in another.  Taken: whether the day was appointed or made for the place where the thing is to be done
-- is an input; yes is TRUE, no is the named refusal.  The other readings are that such a day is a holiday everywhere, and that it is one only
-- in its own place.
-- FORK F-HOLIDAY-BIRTHDAY: "the birthday or the day fixed by proclamation for the celebration of the birthday of the reigning Sovereign".
-- Taken: "or" is plain, so the birthday and a day fixed by proclamation are each a holiday, including when a proclamation fixes a day
-- other than the birthday itself.  The other reading is that a proclamation replaces the birthday for that year.
-- src:309 | holiday means any of the following days, namely, Sunday; New Year’s Day; Good Friday; Easter Monday; Christmas Day; the birthday or the day fixed by proclamation for the celebration of the birthday of the reigning Sovereign; Victoria Day; Canada Day; the first Monday in September, designated Labour Day; National Day for Truth and Reconciliation, which is observed on September 30; Remembrance Day; any day appointed by proclamation to be observed as a day of general prayer or mourning or day of public rejoicing or thanksgiving; and any of the following additional days, namely,
-- src:310 | (a) in any province, any day appointed by proclamation of the lieutenant governor of the province to be observed as a public holiday or as a day of general prayer or mourning or day of public rejoicing or thanksgiving within the province, and any day that is a non-juridical day by virtue of an Act of the legislature of the province, and
-- src:311 | (b) in any city, town, municipality or other organized district, any day appointed to be observed as a civic holiday by resolution of the council or other authority charged with the administration of the civic or municipal affairs of the city, town, municipality or district; (jour férié)
@ref Interpretation Act s 35(1) "holiday" (src:309-311)
GIVEN k IS A `A kind of day`
      `it was appointed or made for the place where the thing is to be done` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`a day of the kind` k `is a holiday under section 35(1) where` `it was appointed or made for the place where the thing is to be done` MEANS
    CONSIDER k
    WHEN `a Sunday`                         THEN TRUE
    WHEN `New Year’s Day`                   THEN TRUE
    WHEN `Good Friday`                      THEN TRUE
    WHEN `Easter Monday`                    THEN TRUE
    WHEN `Christmas Day`                    THEN TRUE
    WHEN `the birthday of the reigning Sovereign` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `the day fixed by proclamation for the celebration of the birthday of the reigning Sovereign` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `Victoria Day`                     THEN TRUE
    WHEN `Canada Day`                       THEN TRUE
    WHEN `Labour Day, the first Monday in September` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `the National Day for Truth and Reconciliation, September 30` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `Remembrance Day`                  THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a day appointed by proclamation to be observed as a day of general prayer or mourning or day of public rejoicing or thanksgiving` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a day appointed by proclamation of the lieutenant governor of a province to be observed as a public holiday or as a day of general prayer or mourning or day of public rejoicing or thanksgiving within the province`
        THEN BRANCH IF `it was appointed or made for the place where the thing is to be done` THEN TRUE
                    OTHERWISE `section 35(1) "holiday" does not say whether a day appointed or made for one place is a holiday for a thing done in another`
    WHEN `a non-juridical day by virtue of an Act of the legislature of a province`
        THEN BRANCH IF `it was appointed or made for the place where the thing is to be done` THEN TRUE
                    OTHERWISE `section 35(1) "holiday" does not say whether a day appointed or made for one place is a holiday for a thing done in another`
    WHEN `a day appointed to be observed as a civic holiday by resolution of the council or other authority charged with the administration of the civic or municipal affairs of a city, town, municipality or other organized district`
        THEN BRANCH IF `it was appointed or made for the place where the thing is to be done` THEN TRUE
                    OTHERWISE `section 35(1) "holiday" does not say whether a day appointed or made for one place is a holiday for a thing done in another`
    WHEN `a Saturday`                       THEN FALSE
    WHEN `any other day`                    THEN FALSE

-- src:309 | holiday means any of the following days, namely, Sunday; New Year’s Day; Good Friday; Easter Monday; Christmas Day; the birthday or the day fixed by proclamation for the celebration of the birthday of the reigning Sovereign; Victoria Day; Canada Day; the first Monday in September, designated Labour Day; National Day for Truth and Reconciliation, which is observed on September 30; Remembrance Day; any day appointed by proclamation to be observed as a day of general prayer or mourning or day of public rejoicing or thanksgiving; and any of the following additional days, namely,
-- src:310 | (a) in any province, any day appointed by proclamation of the lieutenant governor of the province to be observed as a public holiday or as a day of general prayer or mourning or day of public rejoicing or thanksgiving within the province, and any day that is a non-juridical day by virtue of an Act of the legislature of the province, and
-- src:311 | (b) in any city, town, municipality or other organized district, any day appointed to be observed as a civic holiday by resolution of the council or other authority charged with the administration of the civic or municipal affairs of the city, town, municipality or district; (jour férié)
@ref Interpretation Act s 35(1) "holiday" (src:309-311)
GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN a
`section 35(1) "holiday" does not say whether a day appointed or made for one place is a holiday for a thing done in another` MEANS
    REFUSE "section 35(1) holiday does not say whether a day appointed or made for one place is a holiday for a thing done in another"

