§§ `s 35(1) "lieutenant governor"`

-- Plain gloss: for a province, the lieutenant governor or whoever else carries on the province's government, by whatever title; in Yukon,
-- the Northwest Territories and Nunavut, the Commissioner.
-- src:317 | lieutenant governor means the lieutenant governor or other chief executive officer or administrator carrying on the government of the province indicated by the enactment, by whatever title that officer is designated, and in Yukon, the Northwest Territories and Nunavut means the Commissioner; (lieutenant-gouverneur)
@ref Interpretation Act s 35(1) "lieutenant governor" (src:317)
GIVEN p IS A `A province or territory`
GIVETH A STRING
`the office meant by lieutenant governor in` p MEANS
    CONSIDER p
    WHEN Yukon                       THEN "the Commissioner"
    WHEN `the Northwest Territories` THEN "the Commissioner"
    WHEN Nunavut                     THEN "the Commissioner"
    OTHERWISE "the lieutenant governor or other chief executive officer or administrator carrying on the government of the province indicated by the enactment, by whatever title that officer is designated"

§§ `s 35(1) "lieutenant governor in council"`

-- Plain gloss: for a province, the lieutenant governor acting with the advice (or advice and consent, or in conjunction with) the executive
-- council; in Yukon and in the Northwest Territories, the Commissioner acting with the consent of the Executive Council; in Nunavut,
-- the Commissioner.
-- Taken as a convention, not a fork: paragraphs (b) to (d) speak of the territories by name, so they govern there and paragraph (a)
-- governs the provinces.
-- src:318 | lieutenant governor in council means
-- src:319 | (a) the lieutenant governor of the province indicated by the enactment acting by and with the advice of, by and with the advice and consent of, or in conjunction with, the executive council,
-- src:320 | (b) in Yukon, the Commissioner of Yukon acting with the consent of the Executive Council of Yukon,
-- src:321 | (c) in the Northwest Territories, the Commissioner of the Northwest Territories acting with the consent of the Executive Council of the Northwest Territories, and
-- src:322 | (d) in Nunavut, the Commissioner; (lieutenant-gouverneur en conseil)
@ref Interpretation Act s 35(1) "lieutenant governor in council" (src:318-322)
GIVEN p IS A `A province or territory`
GIVETH A STRING
`the person meant by lieutenant governor in council in` p MEANS
    CONSIDER p
    WHEN Yukon                       THEN "the Commissioner of Yukon acting with the consent of the Executive Council of Yukon"
    WHEN `the Northwest Territories` THEN "the Commissioner of the Northwest Territories acting with the consent of the Executive Council of the Northwest Territories"
    WHEN Nunavut                     THEN "the Commissioner"
    OTHERWISE "the lieutenant governor of the province indicated by the enactment acting by and with the advice of, by and with the advice and consent of, or in conjunction with, the executive council"

