§§ `s 35(1) "oath"`

-- Plain gloss: "oath" includes a solemn affirmation or declaration, in the cases and for the persons where one may be made instead of an
-- oath; in those same cases "sworn" includes "affirmed" and "declared".  In other cases the text does not say.
-- src:326 | oath includes a solemn affirmation or declaration when the context applies to any person by whom and to any case in which a solemn affirmation or declaration may be made instead of an oath, and in the same cases the expression sworn includes the expression “affirmed” or “declared”; (serment)
