GIVEN `the person may make a solemn affirmation or declaration instead of an oath, in this case` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`oath includes a solemn affirmation or declaration where` `the person may make a solemn affirmation or declaration instead of an oath, in this case` MEANS
    BRANCH IF `the person may make a solemn affirmation or declaration instead of an oath, in this case` THEN TRUE
           OTHERWISE `section 35(1) "oath" does not say what happens where no solemn affirmation or declaration may be made instead of an oath`

-- src:326 | oath includes a solemn affirmation or declaration when the context applies to any person by whom and to any case in which a solemn affirmation or declaration may be made instead of an oath, and in the same cases the expression sworn includes the expression “affirmed” or “declared”; (serment)
@ref Interpretation Act s 35(1) "oath" (src:326)
GIVEN `the person may make a solemn affirmation or declaration instead of an oath, in this case` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`sworn includes affirmed or declared where` `the person may make a solemn affirmation or declaration instead of an oath, in this case` MEANS
    BRANCH IF `the person may make a solemn affirmation or declaration instead of an oath, in this case` THEN TRUE
           OTHERWISE `section 35(1) "oath" does not say what happens where no solemn affirmation or declaration may be made instead of an oath`

-- src:326 | oath includes a solemn affirmation or declaration when the context applies to any person by whom and to any case in which a solemn affirmation or declaration may be made instead of an oath, and in the same cases the expression sworn includes the expression “affirmed” or “declared”; (serment)
@ref Interpretation Act s 35(1) "oath" (src:326)
GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN a
`section 35(1) "oath" does not say what happens where no solemn affirmation or declaration may be made instead of an oath` MEANS
    REFUSE "section 35(1) oath does not say what happens where no solemn affirmation or declaration may be made instead of an oath"

