§§ `s 35(1) "superior court"`

-- Plain gloss: the courts below, by place, and also the Supreme Court of Canada, the Federal Court of Appeal, the Federal Court and the Tax
-- Court of Canada, wherever the enactment is applied.
-- FORK F-QUEENS: (c) names "the Court of Queen’s Bench for the Province" while the Sovereign is a King.  Taken: the court meant is the
-- province's court of that rank under whatever style the reigning Sovereign gives it, so both names appear in the list for (c).
-- The other reading is that only a court styled "Queen’s Bench" counts, which leaves no court under (c) while there is a King.
-- src:344 | superior court means
-- src:345 | (a) in the Province of Newfoundland and Labrador, the Supreme Court,
-- src:346 | (a.1) in the Province of Ontario, the Court of Appeal for Ontario and the Superior Court of Justice,
-- src:347 | (b) in the Province of Quebec, the Court of Appeal and the Superior Court in and for the Province,
-- src:348 | (c) in the Province of New Brunswick, Manitoba, Saskatchewan or Alberta, the Court of Appeal for the Province and the Court of Queen’s Bench for the Province,
-- src:349 | (d) in the Provinces of Nova Scotia, British Columbia and Prince Edward Island, the Court of Appeal and the Supreme Court of the Province, and
-- src:350 | (e) the Supreme Court of Yukon, the Supreme Court of the Northwest Territories and the Nunavut Court of Justice,
-- src:351 | and includes the Supreme Court of Canada, the Federal Court of Appeal, the Federal Court and the Tax Court of Canada; (juridiction supérieure ou cour supérieure)
@ref Interpretation Act s 35(1) "superior court" (src:344-351)
GIVEN p IS A `A province or territory`
GIVETH A LIST OF STRING
`the superior courts the text names in` p MEANS
    CONSIDER p
    WHEN `Newfoundland and Labrador` THEN LIST "the Supreme Court"
    WHEN Ontario                     THEN LIST "the Court of Appeal for Ontario"
                                              , "the Superior Court of Justice"
    WHEN Quebec                      THEN LIST "the Court of Appeal"
                                              , "the Superior Court in and for the Province"
    WHEN `New Brunswick`             THEN LIST "the Court of Appeal for the Province"
                                              , "the Court of Queen’s Bench for the Province"
                                              , "the Court of King’s Bench for the Province"
    WHEN Manitoba                    THEN LIST "the Court of Appeal for the Province"
                                              , "the Court of Queen’s Bench for the Province"
                                              , "the Court of King’s Bench for the Province"
    WHEN Saskatchewan                THEN LIST "the Court of Appeal for the Province"
                                              , "the Court of Queen’s Bench for the Province"
                                              , "the Court of King’s Bench for the Province"
    WHEN Alberta                     THEN LIST "the Court of Appeal for the Province"
                                              , "the Court of Queen’s Bench for the Province"
                                              , "the Court of King’s Bench for the Province"
    WHEN `Nova Scotia`               THEN LIST "the Court of Appeal"
                                              , "the Supreme Court of the Province"
    WHEN `British Columbia`          THEN LIST "the Court of Appeal"
                                              , "the Supreme Court of the Province"
    WHEN `Prince Edward Island`      THEN LIST "the Court of Appeal"
                                              , "the Supreme Court of the Province"
    WHEN Yukon                       THEN LIST "the Supreme Court of Yukon"
    WHEN `the Northwest Territories` THEN LIST "the Supreme Court of the Northwest Territories"
    WHEN Nunavut                     THEN LIST "the Nunavut Court of Justice"

-- src:352 | telecommunications means the emission, transmission or reception of signs, signals, writing, images, sounds or intelligence of any nature by any wire, cable, radio, optical or other electromagnetic system, or by any similar technical system; (télécommunication)
@ref Interpretation Act s 35(1) "superior court" (src:352)
GIVEN p IS A `A province or territory`
GIVETH A LIST OF STRING
`the superior courts in` p MEANS
    append (`the superior courts the text names in` p)
           (LIST "the Supreme Court of Canada"
               , "the Federal Court of Appeal"
               , "the Federal Court"
               , "the Tax Court of Canada")

§§ `s 35(1) "telecommunications"`

-- Plain gloss: the emission, transmission or reception of signs, signals, writing, images, sounds or intelligence of any nature by any
-- wire, cable, radio, optical or other electromagnetic system, or by any similar technical system.
-- src:352 | telecommunications means the emission, transmission or reception of signs, signals, writing, images, sounds or intelligence of any nature by any wire, cable, radio, optical or other electromagnetic system, or by any similar technical system; (télécommunication)
@ref Interpretation Act s 35(1) "telecommunications" (src:352)
GIVEN `it is an emission, transmission or reception of signs, signals, writing, images, sounds or intelligence of any nature` IS A BOOLEAN
      sys IS A `A system of emission, transmission or reception`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`is telecommunications within section 35(1) where` `it is an emission, transmission or reception of signs, signals, writing, images, sounds or intelligence of any nature` `by` sys MEANS
        `it is an emission, transmission or reception of signs, signals, writing, images, sounds or intelligence of any nature`
    AND CONSIDER sys
        WHEN `a wire system`                   THEN TRUE
        WHEN `a cable system`                  THEN TRUE
        WHEN `a radio system`                  THEN TRUE
        WHEN `an optical system`               THEN TRUE
        WHEN `another electromagnetic system`  THEN TRUE
        WHEN `a similar technical system`      THEN TRUE
        WHEN `a system of none of these kinds` THEN FALSE

§§ `s 35(1) "territorial sea"`

-- Plain gloss: in relation to Canada, the territorial sea of Canada as determined under the Oceans Act, with the airspace above it and the
-- seabed and subsoil below it; in relation to any other state, its territorial sea as determined by international law and its own laws.
-- src:353 | territorial sea,
-- src:354 | (a) in relation to Canada, means the territorial sea of Canada as determined under the Oceans Act and includes the airspace above and the seabed and subsoil below that sea, and
-- src:355 | (b) in relation to any other state, means the territorial sea of the other state as determined in accordance with international law and the domestic laws of that other state; (mer territoriale)
@ref Interpretation Act s 35(1) "territorial sea" (src:353-355)
GIVEN s IS A `A state`
GIVETH A `What a zone is`
`the territorial sea in relation to` s MEANS
    CONSIDER s
    WHEN `Canada as a state` THEN
        `What a zone is`
            WITH `what it is` IS "the territorial sea of Canada"
                 `how it is fixed` IS "as determined under the Oceans Act"
                 `what it also includes` IS LIST "the airspace above that sea"
                                                , "the seabed and subsoil below that sea"
    WHEN `a state other than Canada` THEN
        `What a zone is`
            WITH `what it is` IS "the territorial sea of the other state"
                 `how it is fixed` IS "as determined in accordance with international law and the domestic laws of that other state"
                 `what it also includes` IS EMPTY

§§ `s 35(1) "territory"`

-- Plain gloss: Yukon, the Northwest Territories and Nunavut, and no other place.
