§§ `s 35(1) "writing"`

-- Plain gloss: "writing", or any term of like import, includes words printed, typewritten, painted, engraved, lithographed, photographed,
-- or represented or reproduced by any mode of representing or reproducing words in visible form.
-- FORK F-WRITING: "in visible form" may qualify the whole list or only the last mode, and "includes" does not say that nothing else is writing.
-- Taken: neither side.  Each listed mode, and any other mode of representing or reproducing words in visible form, is TRUE; words not in
-- visible form refuse (S-INCLUDES), because the readings differ on them (a spoken word is out on one and not clearly out on the other).
-- src:360 | writing, or any term of like import, includes words printed, typewritten, painted, engraved, lithographed, photographed or represented or reproduced by any mode of representing or reproducing words in visible form. (écrit)
@ref Interpretation Act s 35(1) "writing" (src:360)
GIVEN m IS A `A mode of representing words`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`writing, section 35(1), includes words in the mode` m MEANS
    CONSIDER m
    WHEN `words printed`           THEN TRUE
    WHEN `words typewritten`       THEN TRUE
    WHEN `words painted`           THEN TRUE
    WHEN `words engraved`          THEN TRUE
    WHEN `words lithographed`      THEN TRUE
    WHEN `words photographed`      THEN TRUE
    WHEN `words represented or reproduced by another mode of representing or reproducing words in visible form` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `words that are not in visible form` THEN `section 35(1) "writing" says what it includes and does not say that words not in visible form are excluded`

-- src:360 | writing, or any term of like import, includes words printed, typewritten, painted, engraved, lithographed, photographed or represented or reproduced by any mode of representing or reproducing words in visible form. (écrit)
@ref Interpretation Act s 35(1) "writing" (src:360)
GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN a
`section 35(1) "writing" says what it includes and does not say that words not in visible form are excluded` MEANS
    REFUSE "section 35(1) writing says what it includes and does not say that words not in visible form are excluded"
